Here is the commit message:
OOZIE-2320
 TestZKXLogStreamingService.testStreamingWithMultipleOozieServers_coordActionList
 is failing (rkanter)

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the query string not being properly decoded before being processed, which could lead to incorrect handling of parameters in the `DummyLogStreamingServlet`. This would result in failures when the test `TestZKXLogStreamingService.testStreamingWithMultipleOozieServers_coordActionList` attempted to stream logs from multiple Oozie servers, as the query string may contain encoded characters that need to be decoded for accurate processing.

Here is the patch:
 import java.io.IOException;
 import java.io.Writer;
+import java.net.URLDecoder;
 import javax.servlet.ServletException;
 import javax.servlet.http.HttpServlet;

 /**
- * Used by {@link TestZKXLogStreamingService#testStreamingWithMultipleOozieServers() } to stream logs from another Oozie "server".
+ * Used by {@link TestZKXLogStreamingService} to stream logs from another Oozie "server".
  * Due to the way the servlet gets loaded, it has to be its own class instead of an inner class.
  */

     @Override
     protected void doGet(HttpServletRequest request, HttpServletResponse response) throws ServletException, IOException {
-        lastQueryString = request.getQueryString();
+        lastQueryString = URLDecoder.decode(request.getQueryString(), "UTF-8");
         response.setStatus(HttpServletResponse.SC_OK);
         Writer writer = response.getWriter();
         writer.append(logs);
         writer.close();
     }
 }


